# Guest Categories

Guest categories help you organize attendees by service level, allowing you to provide differentiated experiences for different groups of guests.

## What are Categories?

Categories are labels you assign to guests that typically represent their VIP status, service tier, or relationship with your organization. Common examples include:

- **AAA** - Top-tier VIP guests (executives, dignitaries, keynote speakers)
- **A** - Priority guests (senior managers, important partners)
- **B** - Standard guests (general attendees)
- **VIP** - Special designation for any tier

Each category can have a unique code, color, and description to help you quickly identify guest groups.

## Category Features

### Category Codes

Each category has a short code (e.g., "AAA", "VIP", "STD") that can be used when importing guests from Excel. The code makes bulk assignment easy - just include a "Category" column in your import file with the category codes.

### Color Coding

Assign a color to each category for visual distinction in the guest table. Colors help you quickly scan the guest list and identify different groups at a glance.

### Service Allocations

Categories can be associated with different service levels, such as:

- Hotel accommodations (star rating, room type)
- Flight class (business, economy)
- Ground transportation (private car, shuttle)
- Seating arrangements

## Using Categories

### During Guest Creation

When adding a guest manually, select their category from the dropdown menu in the guest form.

### Via Excel Import

Include a "Category" column in your Excel file with the category code. The system will automatically assign guests to matching categories during import.

{% callout type="info" %}
Category codes are case-insensitive. "AAA", "aaa", and "Aaa" will all match the same category.
{% /callout %}

### Bulk Reassignment

Use bulk actions to move multiple guests to a different category at once. See the [Bulk Actions](/docs/managing-guests/bulk-actions) guide for details.

## Category-Specific Features

Categories also control:

- **RSVP Form Fields** - Show different form fields to different categories
- **Email Templates** - Create category-specific email templates
- **Reporting** - View RSVP statistics broken down by category
